CREATED:20260313T004136Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260313T004136Z
UID:10007427-1778266800-1778274000@unitedarts.org
SUMMARY:Premier of JazzTales Continued by Trinity Bursey and Gregg Gelb
DESCRIPTION:On May 8\, 2026 at 7 PM join us for the Premier performance of “Lamar the Super Guitar\,” the second installment of the JazzTales series by Trinity Bursey and Gregg Gelb. “Lamar the Super Guitar\,” is a children’s book by Trinity Bursey\, which is illustrated by John Schull and accompanied by a new jazz score by Gregg Gelb and performed live by the Heart of Carolina Jazz Orchestra.  This project is supported by the 2025-26 South Arts Jazz Road Creative Residency and we have support also from the United Arts Council and the town of Knightdale. The story “Lamar the Super Guitar\,” is about kindness. What makes a hero? Lamar thinks it’s daring feats but he will he discover that kindness\, courage\, and showing up are what truly matters this heartwarming\, humorous story which shows young readers how everyday acts of kindness can make a big difference. JazzTales is an interactive storytelling experience that brings books live jazz\, music\, and animation to life\, helping students collaborate and embrace kindness\, and fall in love with stories and music. The evening will also feature a preshow performance by the Knightdale High School jazz ensemble. \nIt’s free and open to the public. \nKnightdale High School \n100 Bryan Chalk Lane\, Knightdale\, NC  27545
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/premier-of-jazztales-continued-by-trinity-bursey-and-gregg-gelb/
END:VEVENT
