UID:10002138-1778331600-1778337000@unitedarts.org
SUMMARY:The Hobbit
DESCRIPTION:Bilbo Baggins\, one of the most reserved of all Hobbits\, is asked to leave his large\, roomy and very dry home in the ground in order to set off as chief robber in an attempt to recover an important treasure. It’s the last thing that any sensitive Hobbit would want to do\, but a great treasure lies in store – not only for Bilbo\, but for all of the Hobbits who inhabit Middle Earth. This 60-minute adaptation of the beloved tale will be a delight to those children and adults who continue to enjoy the magic of Tolkien.\n\n\n\n\nAdapted by Edward Mast\nBased on The Hobbit by J.R.R. Tolkien \nDirected by Flora Bare \nProduced by special arrangement with The Dramatic Publishing Company of Woodstock\, Illinois.
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/the-hobbit/2026-05-09/1/
LOCATION:Raleigh Little Theatre\, 301 Pogue St\, Raleigh\, 27607
ORGANIZER;CN="Raleigh Little Theatre":MAILTO:boxoffice@raleighlittletheatre.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:United Arts Wake County
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260509T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260509T143000
DTSTAMP:20260504T232422
CREATED:20260421T204015Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260505T002611Z
UID:10007479-1778331600-1778337000@unitedarts.org
SUMMARY:Made with Love: A Mother’s Day Bracelet Workshop
DESCRIPTION:A great bonding experience for a mother + child\, join us and learn the basics of hand-stamping metal jewelry in this engaging workshop.\n\n\nA great bonding experience for a mother + child\, join us and learn the basics of hand-stamping metal jewelry in this engaging\, hands-on class at Artspace. In this workshop\, you’ll be introduced to the essential tools\, materials\, and techniques used in hand-stamped metal jewelry. Through demonstrations and guided practice\, you’ll learn how to use metal stamps\, hammer and customize your designs\, and finish your pieces with professional results. \nEach participant will create two metal cuff bracelets using aluminum blanks\, one to keep and one to give! A variety of letters\, numbers\, and decorative symbols will be available so you can personalize your jewelry with meaningful words and patterns. \nAll tools and materials are provided. No experience necessary. The age for this workshop is suitable from pre-teen to 70+. Adult participants will also enjoy some refreshing mimosas\, courtesy of Artspace. \nTickets are sold in pairs and include all materials and drinks. Participants are also welcome to bring their beverage of choice. \nAre you an Artspace member? Email Danny Peña\, Director of Education at dpena@artspacenc.org for your one-time promo code and receive your discount. \n \nAbout the Instructor \nHSIANG-TING YEN’S love of jewelry started at early age. Just like every little girl\, she loved to play with her mother’s jewelry. She was drawn to the fun geometric shapes and the bold colors\, especially the 80s clip resin earrings. Years later\, she began to collect her own jewelry when she was in college. As a maker\, she was fascinated with the idea of making her own jewelry and in 2006 she was introduced to “Beginning Metals and Jewelry” class in her junior year. As soon as she held that jeweler’s saw in her hand\, she knew she had found her calling. \nIn 2012 she received her MA and MFA degrees in Metals and Jewelry from Savannah College of Art and Design. During the three and half year of her graduate school training she created one-of-kind jewelry not only for her loved ones but also for clients that she met at the Philadelphia Museum of Art craft shows. She enjoys the sense of achievement that comes from knowing how much joy her jewelry brings to her clients. She became absorbed with the challenge of problem-solving and brainstorming designs and making the jewelry. She didn’t want to stop\, so in order to continuously share her passion with the world\, she founded Raleigh-based HTY Jewelry in 2013. \nAbout Artspace // \nArtspace is a non-profit visual arts center located in Downtown Raleigh. Visit Artspace to explore exhibitions featuring national and community artists\, engage with more than 35 artists working in their studios\, and enjoy art classes and community events for all ages and abilities. To learn more about Artspace\, visit artspacenc.org \nParking and Accessibility \nFree street parking is available on Davie Street. Parking decks with free weekend parking include: \n\nCity Center Deck\, 429 S. Wilmington St.\nMoore Square Deck\, 233 S. Wilmington St.\nMunicipal Complex Deck\, 201 W. Morgan St.\nWilmington Street Station Deck\, 117 S. Wilmington St.\n\nExplore accessibility information with our Know Before You Go Guide.
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/made-with-love-a-mothers-day-bracelet-workshop/
LOCATION:Artspace\, 201 East Davie Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://unitedarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/e50276bc9793b99f9105379056acb9bf.jpg
END:VEVENT
